  "body": "Found while fixing #3661 (orion-nebula-dev): a group member whose model no account of its provider lists any more (a ZCode Start Plan `GLM-5.3-Trial` after the trial ended) is shown struck on the Routing page with \"No provider serves {id} now; it is skipped\", but the gateway still sends it requests.\n\n- GUI: `internal/gui/assets/plugins/routing/client.js` groupEditor `draw()` strikes a member (`.fbrow.off`) when `modelOf(id)` isn't in `/api/groups`' `models`, which is built from `provider.Served()` (`internal/gui/groups.go`).\n- Gateway: `provider.membersOff` / `resolveIn` (`internal/provider/models.go`) accept any model of an on provider (`lookIn(All(), pid)`), and `perKeyBarred` (`internal/gateway/fallback.go`) returns every account as a candidate when none lists the model (`if len(out) == 0 { return all, … }`).\n\nSo the page says the member is skipped while every request asks it first. After #3661's fix the ZCode plugin's refusal rests only that trial entry, and it is asked again a minute on (a guessed quota rest), so the cost is one local refusal per minute, but the page is still wrong about what happens, and for other vendors an unlisted member costs a real request.\n\nEither the gateway skips a member no account of its provider lists (careful: a plugin's failed list read can drop live entries, e.g. ZCode's gift read failing leaves its `-Trial` entries out; a failed read means unknown), or the page says what the gateway does.\n",
  "closed_by": null,
