   "body": "Fixed on a fork branch: `fix/3805-ready-not-models` (head `848a87ef`, on upstream `6eb510f7`) — a member the gateway routes is not said unserved when the server has it.\n\n**Root cause.** `internal/gui/assets/plugins/routing/client.js`'s editor decided \"no provider serves {id}\" from `modelOf(id)` missing from `groups.models`, while the gateway routes by the member's `ready` flag from `/api/groups` (`internal/provider/groups.go` sets it through `provider.Resolve`) — so a ready member was greyed as skipped and in fact routed.\n\n**Change.** the editor asks the same `ready` the pick row already uses (`info.ready`), so its verdict and the gateway's routing agree; the confirmed case (a member nothing lists, `ready:false`) keeps its badge and wording.\n\n**Verified.** Red: `the new case in `routing-provider-off.test.cjs` (a ready member absent from `models`)` → `routing-provider-off.test.cjs:106: a ready member's editor row is not greyed (true !== false)`\nGreen: `same command → 20/20 (chromium + webkit × en/zh/zh-TW/ja/de × 1100/420); `c/sol` (ready:false) keeps its badge; `TestCoreScriptBudget` unchanged` → `ℹ pass 20, fail 0`\n\nFull `go test -tags nogui ./...` over round 27's branches: 70 packages ok, 5 red (edit `TestWriteAtomicReadOnlyHardLink`, gateway's five, plugin `TestPluginSOCKSProxy`, provider's synctest fatal in `TestUnreadLoginsWriteErrorsKeepCredentials`, testenv `TestProgram`) — every one of them reproduces identically at base `6eb510f7` in this environment (umask 0027), so none is from this change.\n\nBranch: https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/3805-ready-not-models — no PR opened, this repo takes no external PRs; say the word if you'd rather have the patch inline here.",
